      "title": "Northstar Competition Lab — OLBG Tipster Paper Trading",
      "category": "Sports Data & Scoreboards",
      "kind": "app",
      "description": "A deliberately small, evidence-first betting-research workbench built from the Open Betting Exchange prize-money data the user pasted, and its central finding is that none of the strategies beat the market on the pilot sample. A 27-match football pilot (Bundesliga 1 2024/25, matchdays 1, 10 and 20, fixtures committed and sha256-verified) reached 27/27 dual-source result agreement between OpenLigaDB and football-data.co.uk on an exact-minute UK-time join; 405 pre-start odds snapshots (5 providers x 3 selections x 27) were extracted; and four strategies backtested on those real settled outcomes were all negative, the best losing 4.04 units at -36.7 percent ROI with a 95 percent confidence interval including zero. Sport number two is now live: a 21-event ice hockey pilot (DEL 2024/25, matchdays 1, 20 and 40) on the same open-licensed OpenLigaDB results path, with overtime/shootout-aware final-score selection, results treated as available at start plus three hours (inferred, and documented because the community source batch-edited results at end of season), and one strategy `hockey-elo-v1` — a two-way Elo with K=32, home advantage 35 and research priors — that produces predictions only. Its 13 predictions are graded on accuracy, 9 of 13 correct (69.2 percent) with Brier 0.473 by northstar/evaluation.py, while its PnL is reported as unavailable rather than zero, because no permissioned odds path exists for hockey; they are recorded as `unsettleable`, never settled, and kept off the PnL leaderboard by design. Hockey identity is labelled `probable` (single source, no independent DEL cross-check) against football's `verified`. The site shows a verified-odds snapshot feed, an evidence ledger, a PnL leaderboard and a strategy lab; there is a backtest engine (northstar/backtest.py, deterministic walk-forward ordering including same-start event ties), per-strategy modules, a prediction grader, a CLI and report generation. 144 automated offline pytest tests cover fixtures, odds parsing and time-zone handling, settlement, walk-forward invariants and the hockey pilot's guarantees. Every number carries a licence and a retrieval date, and no licensing claim is inherited: the README records that each was re-confirmed verbatim against the live sources on 2026-09-20, and the ODbL attribution requirement for OpenLigaDB is stated on the site itself. Sources retrieved 2026-09-20.",
