      "detail": "The prose-staleness gate reported TradingViewTheLeap behind on the 2026-09-20T04:55Z rebuild: read at b212321, repository now at 6d8f0ef. GET /repos/buffedlizard55-lab/TradingViewTheLeap/compare/b212321...6d8f0ef returns 8 commits and 29 changed files (+26,770/-13,042), headed by ae670a6 'C22 volume-drought ignition model + roster + H41 + verdict set + IR-32/33 + Alpaca source' and c4ffdb6 '60/60 matrix complete; full-pool verdicts H34-H42; C19-A gate fired'. README.md changed by only 20 lines across 65,921 to 66,200 bytes, and every one of those lines is in the leading audit banner: the volatile-stock matrix went from a 37/60 partial pool (16 x 15m, 10 x 1h, 11 x 1d) to a complete 60/60 (20 x 15m + 20 x 1h + 20 x 1d) with byte-level SHA-256 provenance, and a full-pool verdict set was published — H34/H37 partially supported, H36 supported, H35/H38 refuted, H39 (C19) and H41 (C22) inconclusive zero-fire, then the pre-registered gate firing and C19-A registered as H42, also zero-fire and inconclusive. The irregularity is that the body was not updated to match. Grepping the fetched README for `C22`, `C19-A`, `H41` and `H42` returns hits on banner lines 4-6 only; there is no `September 20` or `seventeenth pass` section heading at all, and the newest body section remains 'September 19 sixteenth pass', which still reports the roster as 32 to 38 with C17-C19 and hypotheses H37-H39, still describes 'the 37/60 partial-pool reality', and still gives verification as 401 passed / 0 failed / 1 warning with a 459-check self-test and 94 unit tests. IR-32 and IR-33, named in the commit message, likewise appear nowhere in the README. A reader who takes the roster count, the model list or the verification totals from the body therefore gets the 2026-09-19 state while believing they are reading current documentation — the same failure mode as IRR-51 (VacationSchedule's 16-vs-21 irregularity count), where a summary and the thing it summarises disagree. Both were found by counting and grepping rather than by reading the summary. The description above quotes the banner for capture completeness and verdicts and the body for the sixteenth-pass figures, and says which is which. Note that the banner's own caveat is the important part and is unchanged in substance: captures are Yahoo vendor-tier and not exchange-verified, the Alpaca IEX route (`make official-bars`) is still blocked on environment credentials, and no authenticated TradingView Strategy Report export is available."
